# Nopsai: The Complete Guide

Welcome to the definitive reference for the Nopsai platform. This guide documents how the services cooperate, which features ship today, and how to operate the stack confidently in development or production-like environments.

---

## Platform Vision

Nopsai turns natural-language automation goals into deterministic CI/CD runs. Instead of hand-writing every shell command, teams can describe the outcome they want. The platform combines an AI-powered agent, opinionated pipeline definitions, and rich observability so that automation stays flexible **and** auditable. Real-time feedback, GitHub-native workflows, and secure secret handling are core design pillars.

---

## Architecture Overview

| Component | Highlights |
|-----------|------------|
| **Core API (`services/nopsai`)** | REST and WebSocket surface, pipeline/run lifecycle management, Docker agent orchestration, encrypted secret store, config repo syncing, run grouping, and log archival. |
| **Agent (`services/agent`)** | Executes pipelines inside disposable containers, resolves AI goals, enforces step/task dependencies, masks secrets, and streams granular telemetry to the API. |
| **LLM Agent (`services/llm-agent`)** | gRPC bridge to Google Gemini that produces strongly-typed actions or boolean decisions from execution context. |
| **Git Bot (`services/git-bot`)** | GitHub App webhook handler, rich check-run author, repository data helper, and liaison between Git events and the core orchestrator. |
| **Web UI (`services/ui`)** | Vanilla JS single-page app that consumes REST + WebSocket feeds to present live dashboards, graphs, logs, grouping, and management tooling. |
| **PostgreSQL (`nopsai-db`)** | Durable store for pipelines, reusable steps, triggers, encrypted secrets, environment variables, run metadata, and full log history. |

All services run inside the shared `nopsai-net` Docker network. The agent launches additional per-step containers on the same network so they can reach the LLM agent, git-bot, and any ambient dependencies while keeping each run isolated.

