## Service Deep Dive

### Core API (`services/nopsai`)
- Hosts `/v1` REST endpoints for pipelines, reusable steps, trigger overrides, secrets, environments, run groups, runs, logs, reruns, cancellations, branch clean-up, and Git helper utilities.
- Maintains an in-memory WebSocket hub with per-run subscriptions and global broadcasts (`new_run_started`, `run_update`, `run_summary_update`, `log_line`) so the UI never polls.
- Launches agent containers on demand, mounting a dedicated workspace volume, injecting scoped secrets/environment variables, wiring them into Docker, and tailing logs back into PostgreSQL.
- Encrypts secrets with AES-GCM using a key derived from `NOPSAI_MASTER_KEY`, guaranteeing that sensitive values are protected at rest.
- Syncs pipelines, steps, triggers, and environment definitions from the Git-backed config repository via `/v1/internal/config/sync` or automatically when new commits land.

### Agent (`services/agent`)
- Parses pipeline manifests, expands includes, and builds a dependency graph across steps and nested tasks.
- Supports both scripted tasks and LLM-generated goals, with optional natural-language `condition` checks resolved through the LLM agent.
- Shares a curated directory listing (respecting `llm_content_ignore`) with the LLM, and honours `llm_output_sharing` at pipeline and task granularity.
- Reuses warm step containers, provisions ad-hoc volume mounts, ensures referenced images exist, and injects secrets safely into the environment.
- Streams stdout/stderr in real time, masks secret values before logging, reports status/exit codes/LLM durations per task, and finalises runs through the API.

### LLM Agent (`services/llm-agent`)
- Accepts execution context via gRPC, builds rich prompts that include environment variables, workspace snapshots, execution history, and the requested goal.
- Calls Google Gemini to obtain structured actions (`EXECUTE_COMMAND`, `REPLACE_FILE`, `RETURN_ANSWER`) or to evaluate boolean conditions for pipeline gating.
- Reads runtime configuration (listen addresses, Gemini credentials, logging) from the shared YAML+environment loader, keeping deployment knobs consistent across services.

### Git Bot (`services/git-bot`)
- Validates incoming GitHub webhook signatures, normalises events, and posts run requests to the core API.
- Manages hierarchical check-run state where steps own tasks; renders Markdown summaries or Mermaid diagrams and updates GitHub in real time with progress, failure context, and rerun hooks.
- Offers helper endpoints for repository access checks, file/directory content lookups, pipeline source retrieval, child check-run creation, and stale check-run cancellation.

### Web UI (`services/ui`)
- Boots a resilient WebSocket client that reconnects, resubscribes to active runs, and drives toast notifications whenever `new_run_started` broadcasts fire.
- Provides branch-first dashboards with group/folder organisation, drag-and-drop ordering, inline branch clean-up, run selection for bulk actions, and URL hash deep-linking.
- Renders interactive pipeline graphs with pan/zoom, task cluster expansion, and live status colouring.
- Ships an advanced log modal featuring level chips, agent-only toggle, structured vs. short views, search with navigational controls, copy/download helpers, and follow mode – all backed by WebSocket streaming plus historical fetches.

