## GitHub Integration Workflow

1. Install a GitHub App configured with the git-bot’s externally reachable `/webhook` endpoint and agreed HMAC secret.
2. When events arrive, the git-bot validates the signature, fetches pipeline definitions for the commit, creates or updates the GitHub check run, and asks the core API to start a pipeline run.
3. As the agent advances through tasks, the git-bot streams updates back to GitHub (status, timing, failure context) and exposes rerun/cancel actions.
4. Stale check runs are cancelled automatically when newer commits supersede them, keeping GitHub noise low.

